2026-06-14 feat/transfers-chain — CPO ruling on the PR-i transfers DEDUP (raised by the iteration-3 scope-auditor: which records count as "the same move" is a data-modeling decision needing CPO authority, not builder self-classification). Builder presented the rule plainly; CPO ANSWER (conversation, 2026-06-14, "do it"): dedup to ONE ROW per (player, team_in, team_out, transfer_date) — removing the by-team cross-query duplicate (each move is fetched twice, once per involved club) and exact provider duplicates — WITHOUT fuzzy-merging near-duplicate-date records (the same move emitted a few days apart under different `type`s), since a date-window merge could wrongly fuse two genuine moves. Dedup lives in the BASE layer (base_apif__transfers; staging does NO dedup; core reads the deduped base). league_code is excluded from the dedup partition (a transfer is a global event, deduped across leagues; the surviving league_code is pinned deterministically as ingest provenance). Recorded so the PR-i contract's decisions_taken cites a locatable ruling.

